            <ArticleTitle>Myocardial revascularization in Jehovah Witnesses.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>19-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The refusal of certain patients to accept blood transfusions need not be a deterrent to surgery. We report on nine Jehovah's Witnesses who over a one-year period underwent myocardial revascularization without significant blood loss or decrease in hematocrit values.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
